<p><a href="https://www.charliekurth.com/">Charlie Kurth</a>, currently Professor of Philosophy at <a href="https://www.clemson.edu/cah/academics/philosophy-and-religion/">Clemson University</a>, will be moving to the <a href="https://www.phil.uga.edu/">University of Georgia</a>.</p>
<p><span id="more-58011"></span></p>
<p><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" class="size-full wp-image-58014 aligncenter" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/kurth-charlie-photo.jpg" alt="" width="300" height="218" /></p>
<p>Professor Kurth is known for his work in ethics, philosophy of psychology, and philosophy of mind. He is the author of <em>The Anxious Mind: An Investigation into the Varieties &amp; Virtues of Anxiety </em>(MIT, 2018) and <em>Emotion</em> (Routledge, 2022) as well as many other works. For more information on his publications, see <a href="https://www.charliekurth.com/research">here</a>.</p>
<p>He will be taking up his new position at UGA as Professor of Philosophy and as the first director of UGA&#8217;s <a href="https://franklin.uga.edu/ethics">Ethics Hub</a> in January 2027.</p>
